# Feuerbach's theorem, excircle half — the nine-point circle is externally tangent to the A-excircle: N·Ia = R/2 + ra (source: Feuerbach 1822)
A B C = triangle
O = circumcenter(A, B, C)
N = nine_point_center(A, B, C)
Ia = excenter(A, B, C)
T = foot(Ia, line(B, C))
prove 2 * dist(N, Ia) = dist(O, A) + 2 * dist(Ia, T)
